<commits>
57e6744aae net: count traffic bytes and number of messages globally

Before this change only per-peer stats were gathered. They
are lost when the peer disconnects.

So, collect the traffic stats globally in `CConnman`, broken down by
* direction (sent or received, (2))
* network of the peer (IPv4, IPv6, Tor, I2P, CJDNS (5))
* connection type (inbound, full outbound, feeler, etc, (6))
* message type (verack, ping, etc, (36))

fe609969d7 rpc: visualize global CConnman stats in getnettotals.detailed

Introduce a new field named `detailed` in the output of RPC
`getnettotals` that renders the global traffic stats from `CConnman`.

Co-authored-by: Vasil Dimov <vd@FreeBSD.org>

f33bcc5fd6 test: add functional tests for the new getnettotals.detailed field

Co-authored-by: Vasil Dimov <vd@FreeBSD.org>
</commits>

